        "comments": "The assembly iHemFuc1.1 is based on 88x PacBio data, 88x 10X Genomics Chromium data, and BioNano data generated at the Wellcome Sanger Institute, and Hi-C data generated at the Baylor College of Medicine. The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Falcon-unzip, retained haplotig separation with purge_dups, 10X based scaffolding with scaff10x, BioNano hybrid-scaffolding with Solve, Hi-C based scaffolding and curation carried out at Baylor, Arrow polishing, and two rounds of FreeBayes polishing. The mitochondrial genomes was assembled using MitoHifi. Finally, the assembly was analysed and manually improved using gEVAL. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size.",
